        <mxCell id="qT-E_jMqx8qcXpDc5zsD-8" value="&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;A “logic block” represents a functional group within a module, not a separate Verilog module.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;Connectors with the same name and color represent the same net.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;Bus widths are indicated using range notation, such as [9:0]. Single-bit signals have no range label.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Constants are shown by name rather than by value. Refer to the Verilog source code for their definitions.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=none;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
